    <div class="mwk-content">

        <p>
            Mardon Wale Kaam is an Aatm Nirbhar content series exploring professions traditionally perceived as men's work. Through real-world experiences and conversations with women already working in these roles, the series challenges assumptions about women's participation in different professions.
        </p>

        <p>
            The project extended beyond individual YouTube episodes into a broader content and awareness initiative, with a distribution approach designed to take these stories beyond YouTube and reach relevant audiences.
        </p>

        <h3>CONTENT STRATEGY & CAMPAIGN PLANNING</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Developing the content approach around experience-led storytelling, practical job demonstrations and real women's experiences.</li>
            <li>Structuring the content ecosystem around reach, engagement and lead generation.</li>
            <li>Planning pre-launch, launch and post-launch communication.</li>
            <li>Developing content calendars for teasers, curiosity-driven posts, carousels, short-form clips and episode releases.</li>
            <li>Planning platform-specific content distribution across YouTube, Instagram, Facebook, WhatsApp and LinkedIn.</li>
            <li>Developing a content repurposing approach to extract short-form stories, insights and human-interest clips from full episodes.</li>
            <li>Planning creator and community amplification to extend the series into relevant audiences and women's networks.</li>
            <li>Mapping individual episode clips to relevant Aatm Nirbhar, Scooter Rani, Scooty Didi and founder-led social channels.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>RESEARCH, EPISODE DEVELOPMENT & SCRIPTWRITING</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Researching job roles, processes and practical information for episode narratives.</li>
            <li>Writing Hindi scripts, hooks, presenter narration and episode introductions.</li>
            <li>Structuring job demonstrations and explaining onboarding, registration and work processes.</li>
            <li>Developing interview questions to explore the experiences, challenges, earnings and journeys of the women featured.</li>
            <li>Building episode flow, transitions and storytelling to make each profession accessible to viewers.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>CONTENT DISTRIBUTION & AMPLIFICATION</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Planning short-form content from the full-length episodes for discovery and audience engagement.</li>
            <li>Identifying stories around earnings, safety, work experiences and personal journeys for individual clips.</li>
            <li>Planning community distribution through relevant women's networks and WhatsApp.</li>
            <li>Exploring creator-led amplification, reactions and conversations around women entering traditionally male-dominated professions.</li>
            <li>Connecting content distribution with awareness of livelihood and employment opportunities.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mwk-role">
            My contribution covered content development, research, scripting, campaign and distribution planning, and the structuring of the series into a wider content ecosystem.
        </p>

    </div>

